<% content_for :title, "Campdoc · File delivery with a personal touch" %>
<% content_for :head do %>
  <meta name="description" content="Send files to one person with a note, then know when they open and download them.">
<% end %>

<div class="landing-page">
  <%= render "marketing_header" %>

  <main>
    <section class="landing-hero">
      <div class="landing-hero__copy">
        <h1>The simple way to send files.</h1>
        <p class="landing-lede">Campdoc is the straightforward way to drop a file, add a note, and send it.</p>
        <div class="landing-actions">
          <%= link_to "Send your first file", new_session_path, class: "button button--primary landing-primary-action" %>
          <span>Private by default</span>
        </div>
      </div>

      <div class="handoff-scene" data-controller="handoff" role="img" aria-label="Campdoc sending a contract to Sam, who opens and downloads it">
        <div class="mini-app" aria-hidden="true">
          <div class="mini-app__bar">
            <span class="mini-app__mark">C</span>
            <span>Campdoc</span>
          </div>

          <div class="mini-composer">
            <div class="mini-composer__heading"><span>New send</span><strong>Start with the file.</strong></div>
            <div class="mini-composer__body">
              <div class="mini-dropzone">
                <div class="mini-drop-prompt"><span>↑</span><strong>Drop files here</strong></div>
                <div class="mini-selected-file">
                  <span class="mini-file-icon">PDF</span>
                  <div><strong>Final contract.pdf</strong><small>2.4 MB</small></div>
                </div>
              </div>
              <div class="mini-fields">
                <label>Who’s this for?<span class="mini-field-value mini-field-value--recipient">sam@example.com</span></label>
                <label>Add a note<span class="mini-field-value mini-field-value--note">Here’s the final contract. Let me know what you think.</span></label>
                <span class="mini-send-button">Send file</span>
              </div>
            </div>
          </div>

          <div class="mini-delivery">
            <div class="mini-delivery__intro"><small>Private delivery for Sam</small><strong>You received a file.</strong><p>“Here’s the final contract. Let me know what you think.”</p></div>
            <div class="mini-delivery__file">
              <span class="mini-file-icon mini-file-icon--large">PDF</span>
              <div><strong>Final contract.pdf</strong><small>2.4 MB</small></div>
              <span class="mini-download-button">Download</span>
            </div>
          </div>
        </div>
        <div class="handoff-delivered" aria-hidden="true"><span>✓</span> Sam downloaded it</div>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="landing-manifesto">
      <div class="manifesto-heading">
        <h2>A note about sending work</h2>
      </div>
      <article class="manifesto-letter">
        <p>Hello,</p>
        <p>Sending a file is a small act of trust.</p>
        <p>You made something for someone: a contract, a set of photographs, a draft, or an invoice. The person waiting for it deserves more than a bare download link.</p>
        <p>Most file tools turn this moment into storage work. They ask you to manage folders, permissions, links, and settings. Campdoc has a narrower job. It helps you hand work to one person with the context it deserves.</p>
        <p>You drop the file, add a note, and send it. Campdoc keeps the delivery private and tells you when it was opened and downloaded.</p>
        <p>I want Campdoc to feel like passing a document across a table. You know who has it and what happened next.</p>
        <p>That is what I am building.</p>
        <address class="manifesto-signature">
          <strong>Obakeng Mosadi</strong>
          <%= mail_to "mosadiobakeng7@gmail.com" %>
        </address>
      </article>
    </section>

    <section class="landing-ledger">
      <div class="landing-ledger__copy">
        <p class="eyebrow">After you send</p>
        <h2>Know when it lands.</h2>
        <p>Campdoc records when a Send is opened and downloaded. You can check the handoff without sending another email.</p>
      </div>
      <div class="ledger-card" aria-label="Delivery activity for Final contract.pdf">
        <div class="ledger-file-row">
          <div class="ledger-file-icon">PDF</div>
          <div><strong>Final contract.pdf</strong><span>Sent to sam@example.com</span></div>
        </div>
        <ol class="landing-event-list">
          <li class="complete"><i></i><strong>Sent</strong><span>9:42 AM</span></li>
          <li class="complete"><i></i><strong>Opened</strong><span>10:07 AM</span></li>
          <li class="complete"><i></i><strong>Downloaded</strong><span>10:08 AM</span></li>
        </ol>
      </div>
    </section>

    <section class="landing-cta">
      <div>
        <p class="eyebrow">Your next handoff</p>
        <h2>Start with the file.</h2>
      </div>
      <%= link_to "Send something", new_session_path, class: "button button--primary landing-primary-action" %>
    </section>
  </main>

  <%= render "marketing_footer" %>
</div>
